ription":"Alabama coach Kalen DeBoer said this is the most complete team he's had since taking over for Nick Saban prior to the 2024 season.","published":"2026-11-20T16:07:14.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50541432/kalen-deboer-says-most-complete-alabama-team","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Alex Scarborough","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Can Nebraska's Matt Rhule end his drought against ranked opponents?","description":"Rhule and Nebraska face back-to-back tests against ranked opponents to end the year, marking an opportunity for the Cornhuskers' coach to end a nearly decade-long streak.","published":"2026-11-20T14:02:33.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50534102/nebraska-cornhuskers-matt-rhule-ranked-win-drought","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4918136/quincy-rhodes-jr","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quincy_Rhodes_Jr."},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Quincy Rhodes Jr.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quincy_Rhodes_Jr.","description":"American football player (born 2004)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:37:15Z","intro":"Quincy Rhodes Jr. (born December 1, 2004) is an American college football defensive end for the Arkansas Razorbacks.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Rhodes Jr. attended North Little Rock High School in North Little Rock, Arkansas. As a senior he had 84 tackles and 11.5 sacks. He was selected to play in the 2022 All-American Bowl. Rhodes Jr. committed to the University of Arkansas to play college football."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"Rhodes Jr. spent his first two years at Arkansas as a backup, appearing in 21 games with one start and recording 16 tackles and one sack. He became a full-time starter for the first time his junior year in 2025."}]}}